cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."

title: "Open Citation Trajectory"
abstract: >
  Open Citation Trajectory is an open, reproducible tool for exploring how
  scholarly articles are cited over time. It combines open scholarly metadata
  sources to fetch article metadata, reconstruct citation trajectories from
  OpenCitations, and compare citation counts with OpenAlex, alongside a
  one-click Google Scholar search link.

